.TH "PUSHSUBSCRIPTION.TOJSON" "3JS" "October 30, 2026" "JavaScript" "JavaScript Reference Manual"
.SH NAME
PushSubscription.toJSON \- PushSubscription: toJSON() method
.SH SYNOPSIS
\f[B]Secure context:\f[R] This feature is available only in secure
contexts (HTTPS).
.PP
\f[B]Note:\f[R] This feature is available in Web Workers.
.PP
The \f[B]\f[CB]toJSON()\f[B]\f[R] method of the
\f[CR]PushSubscription\f[R] interface returns a JSON\-serializable plain
object representing the \f[CR]PushSubscription\f[R] object.
.PP
The method is automatically called by \f[CR]JSON.stringify()\f[R] when a
\f[CR]PushSubscription\f[R] object is encountered during JSON
serialization.
.SH SYNTAX
.IP
.EX
toJSON()
.EE
.SS Parameters
None.
.SS Return value
A JSON\-serializable plain object containing the following properties:
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]endpoint\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]expirationTime\f[R]
.IP \(bu 2
\f[CR]keys\f[R]: the \f[CR]p256dh\f[R] and \f[CR]auth\f[R] values
returned by \f[CR]getKey()\f[R], encoded as base64url strings without
padding
.PP
Unless stated otherwise, each property\(cqs value is copied as\-is.
.SH EXAMPLES
.SS Calling toJSON() directly
This example obtains a \f[CR]PushSubscription\f[R] object.
Calling \f[CR]toJSON()\f[R] directly returns a plain object.
Its properties have the same values as the corresponding properties of
the original object.
.IP
.EX
navigator.serviceWorker.ready.then((reg) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
  reg.pushManager.getSubscription().then((subscription) \f[B]=>\f[R] {
    \f[B]const\f[R] json = subscription.toJSON();
    console.log(json); \f[I]// A plain object\f[R]
    console.log(\f[B]typeof\f[R] json); \f[I]// \(dqobject\(dq\f[R]
    console.log(json.endpoint); \f[I]// Same value as subscription.endpoint\f[R]
  });
});
.EE
.SS Serializing to a JSON string
Within the \f[CR]getSubscription()\f[R] callback from the previous
example, the same object can be serialized using
\f[CR]JSON.stringify()\f[R], which calls the \f[CR]toJSON()\f[R] method
automatically.
.IP
.EX
console.log(JSON.stringify(subscription));
.EE
.PP
This would log a JSON string like so (formatted for readability):
.IP
.EX
{
  \(dqendpoint\(dq: \(dqhttps://push.example.com/subscriptions/12345\(dq,
  \(dqexpirationTime\(dq: \f[B]null\f[R],
  \(dqkeys\(dq: {
    \(dqp256dh\(dq: \(dq...\(dq,
    \(dqauth\(dq: \(dq...\(dq
  }
}
.EE
.PP
The base64url\-encoded key values are abbreviated as
\f[CR]\(dq...\(dq\f[R] for readability.
